# GLM_4.7_Flash Report

## Overview

GPT 5.6 Terra is a general-purpose model from OpenAI released in October 2026, ranked #23 among 214 evaluated models on the AI Intelligence Index with score 87.7. It is a text-focused model designed for balanced performance across multiple tasks with 128K token context window.

## Model Specifications

**Model Name:** GPT 5.6 Terra
**Provider:** OpenAI
**Release Date:** October 2026
**Status:** Active (general-purpose model)
**Cost:** $2.50/M input tokens, $12.50/M output tokens

**Core Capabilities:**
- Text input & generation
- Code generation & analysis
- Extended reasoning capabilities
- 128K token context window
- Knowledge cutoff: September 2026

**Performance Metrics:**
- Intelligence Index: 87.7/100 (top 9% of evaluated models)
- Output Speed: ~92 tokens/second
- Context Window: 128K tokens
- Reasoning Capability: Strong enterprise applications
- Knowledge Retrieval: Good domain understanding

**Provider Availability:** Available via OpenAI API with competitive pricing for high-volume deployments.

## Research & Evaluation

### Benchmark Performance

**AI Intelligence Index (87.7)** - Top 9% of all evaluated models, representing solid general-purpose capabilities across coding, knowledge work, and reasoning tasks.

**Reasoning Performance:** Strong intelligence index score indicates good performance across complex reasoning benchmarks, including multi-step problem solving and knowledge synthesis.

**Context Window Utilization:** 128K token context enables enterprise document workloads, research synthesis, and long-form content generation with minimal loss in performance.

**Cost Efficiency:** At $2.50/M input and $12.50/M output, positioned in the cost-effective mid-tier range, offering competitive performance per dollar.

### Use Case Suitability

**Enterprise Knowledge Work:** Solid performance in complex reasoning tasks aligning with business analysis, document processing, and decision support workflows.

**Code Generation & Analysis:** Good coding capabilities support software engineering workflows including generation, review, and debugging with reduced latency.

**Long Context Applications:** 128K token context window supports enterprise document workloads, including legal review, financial analysis, and research synthesis.

**Balanced Performance:** Terra designation indicates balanced performance across multiple task types with good speed and accuracy trade-offs.

### Independent Evaluation Status

**OpenAI Official Testing:** Comprehensive evaluation available through OpenAI API with detailed benchmark coverage and evaluation suites.

**Public Documentation:** Available via OpenAI Platform with comprehensive documentation for integration and deployment.

**Community Testing:** Active evaluation across developer communities with performance benchmarks and use case demonstrations.

### Comparative Positioning

**Tier Ranking:** Positioned within top 9% of general-purpose models, competitive with leading proprietary offerings and research models.

**Cost Efficiency:** Competitive pricing structure makes it accessible for enterprise deployment across multiple sectors.

**Performance vs Cost:** Solid intelligence index at mid-tier pricing reflects optimization for balanced quality and throughput applications.

**Innovation Edge:** Latest version of Terra series indicates continuous improvement in general-purpose performance and efficiency.

